    "id": "/",
    "text": "",
    "title": "MYCC",
    "summary": "## MYCC (Mindmap Knowledge System)\n\nThe MYCC section describes the project's self-description document (`MYCC.md`) and the autonomous knowledge discovery system that transforms it into a structured, LLM-enriched knowledge tree called the **mindmap**. The mindmap serves as the primary memory and discovery mechanism for agents operating within the repository.\n\n### Architecture & Data Model\nThe mindmap is a tree of **Nodes** stored in `.mycc/mindmap.json`.\n- **Node**: Contains a unique `id` (slash-separated path from root), original markdown `text`, a generated `summary`, `title`, `level`, `children`, and `links`. Two in-memory-only flags (`is_mycc`, `is_patch`) — never serialized — track node origin (MYCC.md-sourced vs patch-added) and modification state.\n- **Link**: Directional connections to other nodes (`target_type: 'node'`), local files (`'file'`), external URLs (`'url'`), or project-specific terms (`'term'`). Each has a `comment` describing the relationship.\n- **Terms**: Key project concepts (e.g., \"STAR principle\") marked during exploration and hoisted to the root for fast agent discovery via `recall(path=\"/\")`.\n- **Mindmap**: Top-level structure with `dir`, `source_file`, `hash` (of source markdown), `compiled_at`, `updated_at`, and `root` node.\n\n### Two Independent On-Disk Lines (Redesigned Architecture)\nThe system maintains two separate on-disk artifacts that merge only in memory at load time:\n1. **mindmap.json** — compiled from MYCC.md (foreground, synchronous). Contains MYCC.md-sourced nodes with LLM-generated summaries. Never modified by patches.\n2. **mindmap-patch.jsonl** — append-only JSONL log at `.mycc/mindmap-patch.jsonl` recording structural changes (`add`/`update`/`delete`) from recap sessions. Hash-gated: only actions matching the current mindmap hash are replayed.\n\nAt runtime: load mindmap.json → replay patches → in-memory merged model. The `recall` tool reads this merged tree, displaying `[M]` (MYCC.md-sourced) or `[P]` (patch-added) markers on child nodes.\n\n### Compilation Pipeline\nThe compilation process (`src/mindmap/compile.ts`) is a rotation-based pipeline:\n\n1. **Parsing**: `MYCC.md` is parsed into a hierarchy of sections based on heading levels (code-block-aware — headings inside `` ``` `` are ignored). `src/mindmap/compile-utils.ts` handles parsing, node building, and link extraction.\n2. **Autonomous Exploration**: For each node, an **Explorer Agent** (`src/mindmap/explorer-agent.ts`) is spawned. The agent uses a toolset (`read_file`, `ls`, `grep`, `mark_file`, `web_search`, `web_fetch`, `mark_url`, `mark_term`) to investigate the codebase and external docs. It runs up to 15 rounds, with steering hints when rounds are low, and context compaction (via LLM summarization + transcript save) when token usage exceeds threshold.\n3. **Bottom-Up Summarization**: Summaries are generated from leaves up to the root using the **A-N-C-E context algorithm** (**A**ncestor texts, **N**ode text, **C**hildren summaries, and **E**nvironment guidance), allowing parents to incorporate the summaries of their children. Dependency-aware parallelism with a semaphore (max 3 concurrent LLM calls) ensures children complete before parents.\n4. **Pre-population**: If an old mindmap exists, matching nodes are pre-populated with existing summary/links context to accelerate re-exploration.\n5. **Atomic Rotation**: To prevent data corruption during concurrent access, the system uses a rotation-based save strategy: interim progress saves to `mindmap.json.new`, and on completion: `mindmap.json` → `.bak` and `mindmap.json.new` → `mindmap.json`.\n6. **Lock-Based Resumption**: A lock file (`mindmap.json.lock`) allows the pipeline to resume from the `.new` temp file if interrupted, within a 4-hour freshness window. Stale or hash-mismatched locks are cleaned up automatically.\n7. **Patch Rebuild**: After compile, `/mindmap compile` performs a BFS traversal of the in-memory merged tree to produce a minimal, consistent patch set: one `add` per surviving patch-added node, one `update` per modified MYCC.md node, and one `add` per MYCC.md-deleted node (preserving trimmed content as patch-added knowledge rather than discarding it).\n\n### Patching & Cascading Updates\n- **`patch_mindmap`** (`src/mindmap/patch.ts`): Updates a node's text, then regenerates summaries for all descendants (bottom-up), the target node itself, and all ancestors (from deepest to root) — each via a fresh explorer agent call.\n- **`applyPatchAction`**: Pure in-memory application of a single patch action (no LLM). Sets `is_mycc=false, is_patch=true` for adds; `is_patch=true` for updates (preserving `is_mycc`); removes node for deletes.\n- **`add_child_node`**, **`remove_node`**, **`move_node`**: Structural operations with cascading summary updates.\n\n### Agent Integration & Tooling\n- **`recall` tool** (`src/tools/recall.ts`): The primary interface for agents to query the mindmap by path. At root (`/`), it collects and displays all hoisted terms from descendant nodes. Available to both lead and teammates (scope: `['main', 'child']`).\n- **`/mindmap` slash command** (`src/slashes/mindmap.ts`): Administrative controls — `compile` (with patch rebuild), `get` (query node), `patch` (update text with cascading summaries), `validate` (hash check), `rebuild-patches` (standalone patch dedup).\n- **Validation** (`src/mindmap/validate.ts`): SHA-256 hash comparison between mindmap.json and source markdown; recursive structural validation of nodes and links.\n- **Process Isolation**: Each agent process maintains its own mindmap instance (`.mycc/mindmap.json` for lead, `.mycc/mindmap-{name}.json` for teammates) to avoid race conditions. Cross-process knowledge sharing uses the Wiki (RAG) or mail system, not the mindmap.\n\n### Key Files\n- `MYCC.md`: The authoritative source of truth and project self-description.\n- `src/mindmap/types.ts`: Core type definitions for Node, Link, Mindmap, ANCEContext, MindmapPatchAction.\n- `src/mindmap/compile.ts`: Main compilation orchestration (rotation, lock resumption, parallel summarization).\n- `src/mindmap/compile-utils.ts`: Markdown parsing, node building, link extraction, lock management, ProgressTracker.\n- `src/mindmap/explorer-agent.ts`: Autonomous explorer agent loop with 8 tools, round budget, context compaction.\n- `src/mindmap/load.ts`: Load from JSON, set/strip in-memory flags (`is_mycc`/`is_patch`).\n- `src/mindmap/patch.ts`: Node patching with cascading summary regeneration; `applyPatchAction` for replay.\n- `src/mindmap/patch-jsonl.ts`: Append-only JSONL log for patch actions; `rebuildPatches` BFS dedup.\n- `src/mindmap/get-node.ts`: Tree traversal utilities (get_node, get_ancestors, get_descendants).\n- `src/mindmap/validate.ts`: Hash-based and structural validation.\n- `src/mindmap/diff-mindmap.ts`: Deprecated incremental compile via diff (superseded by rotation-based compile).\n- `src/mindmap/index.ts`: Public API barrel exports.\n- `src/tools/recall.ts`: Agent-facing tool for querying the mindmap knowledge tree.\n- `src/slashes/mindmap.ts`: Slash command interface for mindmap management.\n- `docs/mindmap-design.md`: Original design document (type declarations, A-N-C-E, link stubs, compilation flow).\n- `docs/mindmap-redesign.md`: Redesign document (two on-disk lines, in-memory flags, patch rebuild, recap-to-patch flow).\n- `docs/mindmap-usage.md`: User-facing usage guide (slash commands, recall tool, startup behavior, wiki vs mindmap).",
    "level": 0,
