              {
                "id": "/mycc.md/architecture-core-concepts/grant-system",
                "text": "A permission system for child processes to request approval before performing sensitive operations.\r\n\r\n**Intent Language**: The `bash` tool requires an `intent` parameter in the format `VERB OBJECT PARAM PARAM ... TO PURPOSE`, where VERB is one of READ/WRITE/EDIT/DELETE/BUILD/TEST/INSTALL/RUN and OBJECT is one of SOURCE/CONFIG/DEPENDENCY/ARTIFACT/SYSTEM/DATA/TEMP/USER. Example: `READ SOURCE dir=src TO understand dependencies`. Most PARAMs are free-form; a few reserved PARAMs change routing:\r\n\r\n- **`dangerous=i_know`** — escape hatch for destructive/irreversible commands (e.g., `rm -rf`, force pushes). Declaring it skips the block AND the LLM safeguard, routing directly to the user `[y/N]` — the human's approval is the real authorization. Only affects `destructive`/`irreversible` categories (the `system` category like `git commit` stays hard-blocked — use `git_commit` instead). Unavailable in child processes. Without it, a blocked command returns a Socratic hint naming the *existence* of a PARAM override but withholding the exact key/value. Example: `DELETE DATA path=build/ dangerous=i_know TO reclaim disk space`.\r\n- **`batch=i_know`** — skip the LLM safeguard for batch deletions (multiple files/globs/recursive paths). Routes directly to user `[y/N]`. Only affects the DELETE + batch-delete path (does NOT bypass a hard block, does NOT cover `dangerous=i_know` patterns). Unavailable in child processes. Example: `DELETE TEMP batch=i_know TO clean build artifacts` (for `rm -rf dist/ node_modules/`).\r\n\r\nImplementation: `src/context/grant/bash-judge.ts`. The full system-prompt wording is emitted by `buildIntentLanguageSection()` in `src/loop/agent-prompts.ts`. The `hand_over` tool requires `intent` as `VERB OBJECT TO PURPOSE`; the correct VERB/OBJECT is `RUN USER TO <purpose>` (running an interactive human session) — any other dimension returns a Socratic hint. `command` is a JSON string (multi-line scripts escape newlines as `\\n`, but prefer one-lining with `&&`/`;`/`||`). It refuses to spawn a nested popup if the agent is itself inside tmux. Grant flow: `Child → requestGrant → IPC → Parent → check mode → check worktree → grant/deny`. In `plan` mode: all code changes blocked. In `normal` mode: auto-grant for owned worktree, reject otherwise.",
                "title": "Grant System",
                "summary": "(exploration timeout)",
                "level": 3,
                "children": [],
                "links": [
                  {
                    "target_type": "file",
                    "file_path": "src/context/grant/bash-judge.ts",
                    "comment": "Core 5-step bash command judging logic: dangerous command check, intent validation, mode+verb check, LLM analysis, user confirmation. Implements dangerous=i_know and batch=i_know escape hatches."
                  },
                  {
                    "target_type": "file",
                    "file_path": "src/context/grant/intent-parser.ts",
                    "comment": "Parses and validates intent language (VERB OBJECT [PARAM...] TO PURPOSE). Defines VALID_VERBS, VALID_OBJECTS, read-only/mutation verb classification, and single-pass PARAM tokenizer for malformed PARAM detection."
                  },
                  {
                    "target_type": "file",
                    "file_path": "src/context/grant/dangerous-commands.ts",
                    "comment": "Pattern-based dangerous command detection with three categories: destructive, irreversible, system. Includes indirect-observation wrapper bypass (tmux capture-pane) and execution-wrapper detection (sh -c, eval, $()) to prevent obfuscation."
                  },
                  {
                    "target_type": "file",
                    "file_path": "src/context/grant/grant-evaluator.ts",
                    "comment": "Main grant evaluator dispatching bash to judgeBash and file ops to mode/worktree ownership checks. Handles plan-mode writable directories and worktree-based auto-grant for child processes."
                  },
                  {
                    "target_type": "file",
                    "file_path": "src/context/grant/types.ts",
                    "comment": "Type definitions for the grant system: ParsedIntent, IntentValidation, BashJudgeResult, DangerousCommand, GrantRequest, GrantTool."
                  },
                  {
                    "target_type": "file",
                    "file_path": "src/context/grant/index.ts",
                    "comment": "Barrel export for the grant module — re-exports types, intent parser, dangerous commands, bash judge, and grant evaluator."
                  },
                  {
                    "target_type": "file",
                    "file_path": "src/loop/agent-prompts.ts",
                    "comment": "Contains buildIntentLanguageSection() which generates the full system-prompt wording for the Intent Lang: VERB/OBJECT tables, PARAM syntax rules, examples, and reserved PARAM conventions (dangerous=i_know, batch=i_know)."
                  },
                  {
                    "target_type": "file",
                    "file_path": "src/tools/hand_over.ts",
                    "comment": "Interactive terminal popup tool requiring intent as RUN USER TO PURPOSE. Validates verb=RUN and object=USER with Socratic hints, refuses nested tmux, creates tmux session for human interaction."
                  },
                  {
                    "target_type": "file",
                    "file_path": "src/tools/bash.ts",
                    "comment": "Bash tool implementation that calls ctx.core.requestGrant('bash', {command, intent}) before execution. Enforces timeout 1-60s, blocks direct git commit, truncates large output."
                  },
                  {
                    "target_type": "file",
