        "target_type": "term",
        "term_name": "A-N-C-E",
        "comment": "Context algorithm for generating mindmap node summaries: A (Ancestor texts providing upward hierarchy context), N (Node text being summarized), C (Children/descendant summaries providing downward context), E (Environment/agent behavior guidance for summarization style)."
      },
      {
        "target_type": "term",
        "term_name": "is_mycc / is_patch flags",
        "comment": "Two in-memory-only flags on Node (never serialized to mindmap.json). is_mycc=true for nodes sourced from MYCC.md via mindmap.json; is_patch=true for nodes created or modified by patch actions. Drive compile (only is_mycc nodes get summaries) and patch rebuild (is_patch on is_mycc node → emit 'update' to preserve patched text)."
      },
      {
        "target_type": "term",
        "term_name": "mindmap-patch.jsonl",
        "comment": "Append-only JSONL file at .mycc/mindmap-patch.jsonl recording structural changes (add/update/delete) from recap sessions. Replayed at load time to rebuild the in-memory merged tree. Hash-gated: only hash-matching actions are replayed. Rebuilt during /mindmap compile via BFS dedup."
      },
      {
        "target_type": "term",
        "term_name": "atomic rotation",
        "comment": "File rotation strategy during mindmap compilation to prevent data corruption: mindmap.json → mindmap.json.bak (backup), mindmap.json.new → mindmap.json (atomic rename). Interim progress is saved to the .new file, not the main file."
      },
      {
        "target_type": "term",
        "term_name": "lock-based resumption",
        "comment": "Lock-based mechanism allowing interrupted mindmap compilations to resume from the temp file (.new) within a 4-hour freshness window. The lock file records start time, source file, source hash, and output path."
      },
      {
        "target_type": "term",
        "term_name": "patch rebuild",
        "comment": "BFS traversal of the in-memory merged tree during /mindmap compile that produces a minimal, consistent patch set: one 'add' per surviving patch-added node, one 'update' per modified MYCC.md node, and one 'add' per MYCC.md-deleted node (preserving trimmed content as patch-added knowledge)."
      }
    ]
  }
